Upstream installs libKGlobalAccelD.so.0 and libKGlobalAccelD.so.6.8.0 only
(LIBRARY NAMELINK_SKIP), since consumers are expected to use the exported
K::KGlobalAccelD target with its absolute IMPORTED_LOCATION.

For cross builds the KDE GCC_WRAPPER_FILTER (package/kde/kcoreaddons/kde-conf.in)
rewrites absolute $root library paths back to -l<name>, which then fails:

  ld: cannot find -lKGlobalAccelD: No such file or directory
  make[2]: *** [src/CMakeFiles/kwin.dir/build.make:7051: bin/libkwin.so.6.8.0] Error 1

Install the development symlink like every other shared library so the
-l<name> form resolves.

Signed-off-by: René Rebe <rene@exactco.de>

--- kglobalacceld-6.8.0/src/CMakeLists.txt.vanilla
+++ kglobalacceld-6.8.0/src/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -58,4 +58,4 @@ install(FILES
   DESTINATION ${KDE_INSTALL_INCLUDEDIR}/KGlobalAccelD/ COMPONENT Devel
 )
 
-install(TARGETS KGlobalAccelD EXPORT KGlobalAccelDTargets ${KF_INSTALL_TARGETS_DEFAULT_ARGS} LIBRARY NAMELINK_SKIP)
+install(TARGETS KGlobalAccelD EXPORT KGlobalAccelDTargets ${KF_INSTALL_TARGETS_DEFAULT_ARGS})
